<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Torrijos–Carter Treaties</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1977">1977</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Torrijos–Carter Treaties were two agreements signed on 7 September 1977 by Panama's leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/omar-torrijos">Omar Torrijos</a> and US President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jimmy-carter">Jimmy Carter</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/panama-canal">Panama Canal</a> Treaty abolished the Canal Zone in 1979 and provided for joint administration until the canal passed fully to Panama on 31 December 1999, while the Neutrality Treaty guaranteed the canal's permanent neutrality. They were approved by a Panamanian plebiscite and narrowly ratified by the US Senate in 1978.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/torrijos-carter-treaties.jpg" alt="Torrijos–Carter Treaties" width="320" height="218" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: White House photo · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jimmy_Carter_and_General_Omar_Torrijos_signing_the_Panama_Canal_Treaty.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
